@meta
id: 24-07
title: Drill — copy the template row
chapter: 24
type: drill
skills: ex-copy
par: 11
minutes: 3
reps: 8
vscode: click line 2, Home, Shift-End, Ctrl-C, Ctrl-End, Enter, Ctrl-V
open: customers.csv

@brief
Eight times: line 2 is the template row. Append a copy of it to the end
of the file. One command, no cursor movement.

@keys
| `:2t$` | copy line 2 to the end of the file |

@hints
Range is the source line, destination is the last line.
--
`:2t$` and Enter, then `:wq`.

@solution
    :2t$<Enter>  :wq<Enter>

Nine keystrokes. `2GyyGp` is the same length and leaves you at the
bottom of the file holding a copy in the unnamed register. `:2t$` leaves
you where you were and touches nothing. When the source is at line 2
and you are at line 400, the difference is a round trip.

@start customers.csv
id,email,name,tier
cus_500,template@example.com,Template Customer,standard
cus_501,ana@example.com,Ana Ruiz,gold
cus_502,ben@example.com,Ben Okafor,standard
cus_503,cho@example.com,Cho Min-jun,silver

@expected customers.csv
id,email,name,tier
cus_500,template@example.com,Template Customer,standard
cus_501,ana@example.com,Ana Ruiz,gold
cus_502,ben@example.com,Ben Okafor,standard
cus_503,cho@example.com,Cho Min-jun,silver
cus_500,template@example.com,Template Customer,standard
